\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's Sol Strengthens Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Stocks Rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2004\par 22:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol closed stronger Thursday, despite Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy a record $83 million.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been gaining ground on strong economic fundamentals and a perception that the dollar could continue weakening.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.3620 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.3610-PEN3.3630.  \par \par \uc2 The sol had closed the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.3765 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.3760-PEN3.3770.  \par \par \uc2 "We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid volatility," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Javier Silva Ruete told television station Canal N.  \par \par \uc2 "We don't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  just because the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is rising or falling. We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy at cheap prices and increase our international reserves," he added.  \par \par \uc2 As of Aug. 17, Peru's net international reserves increased $970 million since the year began.  \par \par \uc2 "There are expectations that the sol will strengthen even more and as long as there these expectations, it will continue to strengthen," a trader at Banco Wiese Sudameris said.  \par \par \uc2 The government has come under pressure to limit strength in the sol in order to help exporters.  \par \par \uc2 Silva Ruete, however, pointed out that Peru has been reaching record export levels, which has helped the Andean nation run large trade surpluses.  \par \par \uc2 Peru's exports in the January to July period totaled $6.52 billion, a 30% rise from the same period a year before.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday also placed PEN80 million in one-year certificates of deposit at an average annual yield of 4.54%, and another PEN80 million in nine-month CDs at an average annual yield of 4.17%.  \par \par \uc2 The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 2.63% on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Lima's stock indexes ended higher Thursday as Buenaventura SAA and a number of small shares gained ground.  \par \par \uc2 The general index rose 0.21%, or 5.89 points, to end at 2,850.47.  \par \par \uc2 The selective blue chip index increased 0.29%, or 13.68 points, to end at 4,723.32.  \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner Buenaventura SAA rose 2.0% to end at PEN77.00 as gold prices increased.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 08-26-04 1646ET ]  \par \par \uc2 1071 1837  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020040826e08q00041\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
