\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Sol Strengthens; Stock Indexes Higher  \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 23:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's sol strengthened Monday on renewed interest in the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4600 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4590-PEN3.4610.  \par \par \uc2 The sol closed the previous trading session at a midrate of PEN3.4615 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4610-PEN3.4620.  \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bought $10 million. So far this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $642.5 million.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also placed PEN100 million in 1-week CDs at an average annual yield of 2.59% and auctioned PEN40 million in 12-month certificates of deposit at an annual average yield of 3.40%.  \par \par \uc2 The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 2.48% on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Lima's stock indexes ended higher Monday, spurred by rising metals prices.  \par \par \uc2 The broad General Index closed 21.23 points, or 0.72%, higher at 2974.10.  \par \par \uc2 The blue chip Selective Index rose 49.03 points, or 0.97%, to end at 5089.23.  \par \par \uc2 Southern Peru Copper Corp. gained 2.4% to end at $39.00 on rising copper prices. Tin miner Minsur SAA also continued its steady climb when investors were encouraged by a jump in tin prices. The share gained 8.9% to end at PEN8.84.  \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 03-29-04 1627ET ]  \par \par \uc2 1071 1837  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020040329e03t0003s\par }\page