\par\par \b \uc2 Market uncertain about Peru cenbank's  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  policy.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Marcel Deza   \par \uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2003\par 20:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 21 (Reuters) - Heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has slowed an appreciation of the nuevo sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and led to market uncertainty over the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, analysts and traders said on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's formal policy is to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float freely, buying or selling dollars in the market only to prevent volatility.   \par \par \uc2 Yet it has dramatically stepped up its purchases of dollars in the market this year, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has firmed 1.0 percent between January and October on an upbeat economic outlook.   \par \par \uc2 Traders are left wondering who sets the exchange rate - the market or the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank's purchase of $699.7 million to date this year compared with $95 million last year, when the sol depreciated 2.4 percent and was hit by a financial crisis in Brazil.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  causes surprise since there is no volatility in the market. Or is the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  defending a certain level?" said one trader who asked his name be withheld.   \par \par \uc2 "They're not letting the exchange rate follow the logical trend it would follow, according to market flows," said another trader.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its dollar purchases aim only to provide liquidity to the Public Treasury for paying short-term debt.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have an exchange rate target and its policy is characterized as flotation. It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to avoid jumps and dramatic falls in the exchange rate or to attend to government \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 One trader said the sol, which has traded recently at around 3.48 soles per dollar, would have strengthened to 3.44 per dollar without the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "There are several factors making demand for dollars unattractive. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float freely, the sol would have strengthened more," said Mario Guerrero, analyst with Banco Wiese Sudameris.   \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the sol traded at 3.478 per dollar at midsession. The government expects the exchange rate to finish 2003 at 3.50 soles and hover around 3.59 soles per dollar in 2004.   \par \par \uc2 Stability in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , advances in the development of Peru's Camisea gas project and domestic support for the government's tax reforms have all helped ease investor demand for safe-haven dollars and bolster the sol.   \par \par \uc2 The government forecasts economic growth this year of 4 percent and a growing trade surplus.   \par \par \uc2 Other financial market players suspect the bank wants to prevent the sol from firming to the point where it hurts exporters.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is doing what it has always done: avoid an appreciation of the sol that affects the competitiveness of exports in the face of strong pressures to appreciate," said an analyst with Apoyo consultancy.   \par \par \uc2 Peru is a leading exporter of gold, copper, fishmeal, fish and zinc.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031021dzal0032r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
