\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Sol Ends Stronger; Stock Market Closes Higher \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2003\par 23:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's sol ended stronger Monday in low volume trading despite a fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which purchased $15.0 million, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased dollars for 18 consecutive trading sessions. \par \par \uc2  It has bought $323.7 million so far this year. \par \par \uc2  The sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4573 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4570-PEN3.4575 to the dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The sol closed Wednesday at a midrate of PEN3.4583 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4581-PEN3.4585 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Companies purchased soles to pay their taxes and banks sold their excess of dollars, an analyst said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also auctioned PEN70 million in overnight repurchase agreements, or repos, at an average yield of 3.71%. \par \par \uc2  The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 3.82% on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was closed Thursday and Friday for Easter Holidays. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Lima's stock indexes closed higher Monday as a wide-range of shares rose. \par \par \uc2  The broad general Index closed 22.50 points, or 1.33% higher at 1713.50. \par \par \uc2  The blue chip Selective Index closed 41.49 points, or 1.56%, higher at 2694.82. \par \par \uc2  Financial holding company Credicorp Ltd rose 0.3% to end at $10.30, while Banco Wiese Sudameris, Peru's third largest, rose 7.1% to end at PEN0.15. \par \par \uc2  Various mining companies also gained. \par \par \uc2  Copper producer Southern Peru Copper Corp rose 1.3% to end at $15.60, while tin miner Minsur SAA gained a sharp 3.9% to end at PEN4.00 in heavy trade. \par \par \uc2  Zinc miner Volcan SAA rose 4.2% to end at PEN0.25. \par \par \uc2  The stock market was closed on Thursday and Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020030421dz4l005pl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
