\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Stock Market Ends Mixed; Sol Stronger \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2003\par 23:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's sol ended at its strongest point of the year on Friday, even as the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $15.0 million, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought dollars for 14 consecutive trading sessions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $268.7 million so far this year. \par \par \uc2  The sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.4628 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4625-PEN3.4630 to the dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The sol closed the day before at a midrate PEN3.4663 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4660-PEN3.4665 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed PEN50 million in one-year certificates of deposit at an average rate of 4.58%. \par \par \uc2  The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 3.79% on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Lima's stock indexes closed mixed Friday as miner Bueaventura SAA rose. \par \par \uc2  The broad general Index closed 0.80 point, or 0.05%, higher at 1654.32. \par \par \uc2  The blue chip Selective Index closed 3.96 points, or 0.15%, lower at 2589.04. \par \par \uc2  Precious metals miner Buenaventura SAA ended 0.4% higher at PEN45.18 on stronger gold prices. \par \par \uc2  Financial holding company Credicorp Ltd. rose 0.5% to end at $10.50. \par \par \uc2  -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020030411dz4b009kh\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \pa